    "result_text": "The acceptance tests are the entire suite. The change is complete and the full test suite is green (42/42 passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional, city-region-validated owner postcodes on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Behavior implemented (per spec):**\n- A 4-digit `postcode` is validated **only when present**; absent \u2192 owner still accepted (contract stays backward-compatible).\n- Valid postcode is **stored and returned** (visible via `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n- Range is keyed off the city's region (via the existing `OwnerLocality` table): NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099.\n- A city with **no known region** (`UNKNOWN`) accepts any 4-digit postcode.\n- Malformed (not 4 digits) or out-of-range postcode \u2192 **400 Bad Request**.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added `postcode` column + getter/setter.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added optional `postcode` to `OwnerFields` (flows into generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`; MapStruct maps it automatically by name).\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 added `validatePostcode(...)` (called in `addOwner`) with the region\u2192range table.\n- `rest/controller/InvalidPostcodeException.java` \u2014 new exception (mirrors `InvalidTelephoneException`).\n- `rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` \u2014 new handler mapping it to 400.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql` \u2014 added `postcode` column (tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema column was required).\n\n**Tests:** `Cp29Tests` (postcode) and `Cp13Tests` (uses distinct postcodes) pass; full suite is 42/42 green.",
